      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Goodale Homestead, built in 1702, is Hudson’s oldest surviving building and once served as a stop on the Underground Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hudson%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1979 Digital Equipment Corporation opened the Hudson Fab semiconductor plant, marking the town’s shift to high‑technology manufacturing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
